2003-10-15  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* syntax.h: Variable::generate_code() now generating proper MOV
	instruction for startevent (though still hardcoded with strings).

	changed code generation for constant pattern so that, in case of failure,
	it jumps to next label (and not current one!).

	* display.cpp (display_instruction): added JMP_INSN

	* parse.cpp: registered unary_instruction JMP

	* exec.cpp: added execution for JMP_INSN

	* instructions.h : added absolute jump: JMP_INSN

	* generate.cpp: prepare_non_primitive_call() now generates the
	move instruction to the correct typed register when returning from
	call.

	* syntax.cpp: changed LetExpression::generate
	so that type is passed as argument.

	* unassembled.h: 
	    - changing get_next_num for ENTER->0
	    - changing get_next_num for MOV_P->2
	    

2003-06-11  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* syntax.h: swapped order of code generation in conditional, else first
	then second.

	changed the recursive call of Application::construct_frames() so
	that it operates or rator and operands (and not on function and arguments
	which are prenormalisation!).

2003-06-04  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* syntax.h: added support for an Icode and C++ label in
	  the frame generated for a combination
	  
	  added a surroundFrameGeneratingConstruct for IntValue
	  added stack dropping in terminal position when returning
	   an intValue (as for variable)

2003-05-28  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* unassembled.h: in macro_expansion of MOV_E, I defined
	the frame_a and frame_b variables for the expanded code,
	so that stack offsets size can be computed.

	initilise environment to false in Spb constructor.
	

	added TAG_SIZE

	changed emit for addressing such that environment=1 so
	that WORD_SIZE is added to size (instead of 1)

	* generate.cpp:  computeTypeSize(char* s) computes the space
	required by a given type.
	

	* exec.h (bytecode_enter): redefined enter into bytecode_enter

2003-05-21  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* unassembled.h: ENTER_insn now has one
	successor: it is the DROPPED directive that will stop the
	frame propagation analysis.
	

	* syntax.h: in Module define the resultType of the lambdaExpression

	construct_local_frames: adds a label argument

	reorder the BRA instruction in code generated for conditional

	* unassembled.h: changed second argument to environmentizeArgument
	so that it is not the copy altered by parsing.

	changing spB, indexed register, and celle registor so that they
	support environmentize like Spa, simply because we can get
	closures allocated on spB

	changing closure so that it supports a frameA size (therefore it
