	* unassembled.h (computeOffset): parse the arguments of the new
	indexing modes cell and ptr and compute offsets.

	* exec.h (_revaluate2): adding support for PTR_MODE and CELL_MODE 

2003-02-19  Luc Moreau  <L.Moreau@ecs.soton.ac.uk>

	* unassembled.h: added new addressing modes
	CELL and PTR

	* parse.cpp: added new registers ptr, ptrEnv and addressing modes
	CELL and PTR

	* unassembled.h: macro expansion of MOV_E properly
	handles environments!
	
	In FRAME_insn, there is now a method supposed
	to compute the index of a variable in the stack.
	Currently, it assume a constant word size for all types!

	adding a computeOffset for b stack reference.

	spA changed to support internal flag, indicating if we talk about
	expression or environment.

	 in DRA, size of frame was multiplied by two because an Expr is
	 two pointers!

	* exec.cpp: MOV_P_INSN was fixed to _unary_exec(PTR,)
	instead of _unary_exec(int,);

	* unassembled.h: added support for frame analysis and relative
	label for GTE.

